# sha256 manifest for pinned/ -- the frozen pipeline contract input.
#
# Hash covers LF-canonical content (CRLF normalised to LF) so the manifest is
# checkout-independent: .gitattributes sets `* text=auto`, which rewrites line
# endings on checkout under core.autocrlf=true. Hashing raw bytes would make
# this gate pass in one working tree and fail in a fresh clone or on Linux.
#
# Regenerate ONLY when intentionally re-pinning:
#   python tools/dui-pipeline/ci_checks.py hash --write
# Format: <sha256>  <path relative to pinned/>  (sorted, LF, lowercase hex)
e4c6d33987b97e9fcae32fa8e8e07f891f8c34a7de82d170fb54eebd7a8820c8  class-inventory.csv
a1243457858f2ce1662d9f90fb33650a0dfed8950d23b3505118d8ac1a3d6873  classes.json
3634ee413550ceb75b204ead44da7d5e462256eb2d5b43cde2e30381d4690e81  exports.json
068da6ad1ffa42d501e3db84d311ec50e9894d146cb018ad2dc258b3174ee652  manifest.json
